{"nodes": [{"id": "devtools_ui_src_panels_dashboard_dashboardpanelcomponent_overview_panel", "label": "Overview panel", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "devtools-ui/src/panels/dashboard/DashboardPanelComponent.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "devtools_ui_src_panels_dashboard_dashboardpanelcomponent_span_selection", "label": "Per-option binding for the charted span", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "devtools-ui/src/panels/dashboard/DashboardPanelComponent.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Selection is bound per option rather than as a value on the select: the value is applied before the loop has produced the options, the browser falls back to the first one, and the control then disagrees with the span the panel is actually charting (#485)."}, {"id": "devtools_ui_src_panels_dashboard_dashboardpanelcomponent_per_node_breakdown", "label": "Per-node breakdown hidden below two nodes", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "devtools-ui/src/panels/dashboard/DashboardPanelComponent.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A breakdown of one is the totals with extra steps; it appears the moment a cluster has a second member, which is also the moment the totals stop telling you WHERE something is happening."}, {"id": "devtools_ui_src_panels_dashboard_dashboardpanelcomponent_chart_peak_legend", "label": "Peak reading in the chart legend", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "devtools-ui/src/panels/dashboard/DashboardPanelComponent.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "ECharts has no peak reading, and it is the one number that makes two charts comparable at a glance."}, {"id": "devtools_ui_src_panels_dashboard_dashbo